                <pb facs="0201" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-16T16:00:00-05:00">November 16, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. Your 24, November 10, 6 p.m., penultimate paragraph. There is no present
                    prospect of a repeal or a suspension or a modification of the existing
                    neutrality legislation and you should proceed on the assumption that no such
                    action will occur.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
